      source: "Engraved portrait of Bernardino de Sahagun, captioned 'BERNARDINO DE SAHAGUN.', page 375 of Fanny Chambers Gooch Iglehart, 'Face to Face with the Mexicans' (New York: Fords, Howard and Hulbert, 1887), from the University of North Carolina at Chapel Hill copy digitised by the Internet Archive. A posthumous nineteenth-century engraving whose engraver and source image the book does not name, made about 300 years after his death; not a lifetime likeness. The file is a crop of the plate and its caption from the full page scan (1747 x 2620), 520 x 910, no upscaling; the left shoulder is clipped slightly to avoid adjacent text.",
