      // [src_puskas_footballtimes, src_puskas_realmadrid, src_puskas_fifa | 1958-1966 | football-history feature + club page + governing-body feature] These Football Times says he accepted that Di Stefano was the star at Real Madrid and, in the last game of his first season when both were level as top scorers, rounded the goalkeeper and passed across an open goal for Di Stefano; the club page credits his gentlemanliness and friendliness; FIFA records Hidegkuti praising him and Puskas describing the Golden Team as one in which everyone attacked and everyone defended (his own words, self-report). The pass is a single anecdote from one feature, and the praise is largely retrospective, so confidence is low.
