      source: "Printed plate captioned 'Portrait of Hiraga Gennai' (Hiraga Gennai shozo) in Kakurin Yashi, Hiraga Gennai (Tokyo: Kobunkan, 1899), as digitised by the National Diet Library (NDL Digital Collections item 888008, IIIF canvas R0000003). It is a line-and-halftone print of a seated man in a dark robe holding a long curved fungus-shaped staff, with a small artist's seal at the lower left that cannot be read; the draughtsman is not named in the metadata. The scan of the book spread (3802 x 2929 pixels) carries library ownership stamps, which were left out by cropping to the picture only (1264 x 1640 pixels), then reduced to 925 x 1200 pixels; no upscaling, no retouching.",
