      source: "Stipple engraving 'Ignatius Sancho' by Francesco Bartolozzi after Thomas Gainsborough's oil portrait, lettered 'Gainsborough Pinxt.' and 'F. Bartolozzi sculp.' and published in London on 20 December 1802 by William Sancho, Charles Street, Westminster; The Metropolitan Museum of Art, Harris Brisbane Dick Fund, 1917 (17.3.756-2151, object 376537). The museum's image (2158 x 3482) was cropped to the oval plate with its title line and downscaled to 862 x 1200 with no upscaling.",
